  "body": "`edit_machine {\"edm\":{\"codes\":{...}}}` is refused: \"unknown key 'edm.codes'\", yet the wire-iso post fails with \"machine ... states no edm.codes.condition / comp_off / thread / cut / tip_disposal - the wire post never invents an EDM code\". `get_job` shows them under a top-level `edm_codes`. Workaround: write a .mch file and load it.\n\nDone means: edit_machine sets (and get_job shows) the wire EDM codes under one consistent key; a test sets them and posts through wire-iso.\n\nFound in a wire EDM validation run of CamCraft 0.24.0 through the camcraft MCP (2026-11-21), on test parts in `~/Desktop/camcraft/edm-validation/` (EDM-T1 square, EDM-T2 2-axis block, EDM-T3 taper block) and a Sodick owner's own UV part (spikeypineapple, #617). Wire EDM-W025 (0.25 mm), Sodick ALC400G with test conditions.",
